  "notes": {
    "jdk-collection": "`items` is a java.util.List<Item>, so `items.add(item)` / `items.size()` / `out.add(...)` are JDK methods. Repo.add calling items.add must not become a Repo.add self-loop, nor link to AuditedRepo.add.",
    "super-call": "`super.add(item)` in AuditedRepo.add is Repo.add, never AuditedRepo.add itself.",
    "virtual-this": "Unqualified `add(i)` in AuditedRepo.addAll is this.add, which AuditedRepo overrides; no subclass of AuditedRepo exists, so the runtime target is AuditedRepo.add.",
    "same-package-subtype": "AuditedRepo extends Repo from the same package (no import). `validate(item)` is inherited, declared only in Repo.java.",
    "inherited-method": "`repo` is an AuditedRepo; size() is not overridden, so the target is Repo.size in Repo.java.",
    "typed-field": "Field `AuditedRepo repo`, so `repo.add` is AuditedRepo.add (the override), not Repo.add.",
    "wildcard": "`import com.acme.core.util.*;` makes every type of the package visible. IMPORTS lists every file of that package in the built modules (Log.java, Strings.java under core/), never the vendored third_party copy.",
    "vendored-duplicate": "third_party/acme-util holds another com.acme.core.util.Strings (same FQCN). The parent pom does not list it as a module and no module depends on it, so it is never on the compile classpath: Strings.slug from app binds to core/.../util/Strings.java. The vendored file's own internal call (slug -> collapse) is still a real same-class call.",
    "interface-dispatch": "`notifier` is declared as the interface Notifier. The compiler binds the call to Notifier.send (Notifier.java, abstract); at run time it dispatches to EmailNotifier or SmsNotifier depending on the injected object (App injects EmailNotifier, but OrderService alone cannot know). All three files are plausible targets.",
    "nested-static-import": "`import static com.acme.core.config.Settings.Defaults.pageSize;` and `import com.acme.core.config.Settings.Defaults;` both name the nested class Defaults inside Settings, which lives in Settings.java (the first capitalised segment picks the file).",
    "same-package-no-import": "App, OrderService and Report share package com.acme.app; no import needed. Report is package-private.",
    "test-source-root": "RepoTest is in core/src/test/java but declares package com.acme.core.repo, the same package as Repo (different source root, same package).",
    "multi-module": "Maven reactor: core and app are modules; app depends on core. Imports from app resolve into core/src/main/java by FQCN.",
    "scope": "Constructor invocations (`new Item(...)`) are not listed as calls. Imports of JDK / JUnit types are external and not listed."
  }
}
